meta {
  name: Stop sandbox
  type: http
  seq: 52
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sim/players/:sessionId
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  sessionId: 250
}

docs {
  200 { stopped: true, sessionId, abandoned: true }
  404 { error }   // nothing is sailing this session

  Todo 63 — stop the loops, drop the scripts and ABANDON the session.

  Abandoning is the default on purpose: a half-sailed simulated race has no run
  for at least one boat, so it derives `live` for ever, never freezes a table and
  keeps blocking its boats. Stopping without closing the record would just
  recreate the session-250 pattern this feature was written around.

  The tracks and any runs already uploaded stay — that is what makes the stop
  inspectable rather than destructive. Sweep the session later with
  `node tools/prune-db.js --sim-sessions --yes`.

  Default id 250 is the leftover scratch session from the 56 bench round. Ids are
  autoincrement and do not restart at 1; a stale id answers 404, which is the
  route being right.
}
